				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>S.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Veniam peto, amicorum optime, si requiro, quod praestare sine tuorum negociorum ia<lb xml:id="p1z2"/>ctura non potes.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Equidem proximis nihil petii propter me, sed propter eos, qui <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>me rogant de veritate rerum, quę <placeName ref="l587">Tiguri</placeName> solent evenire<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1">Vgl. oben <ref target="file11797">Nr. 1751</ref>, 15-21.</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Deinceps ero prudentior.</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z4"/>Historiam interea de monacho rufo<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Unbekannt (vgl. ebd., Z. 16-19).</note> multo libentissime audivi.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">Tu si posses <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>eodem animo de <persName ref="p4518">Petro Caroli</persName> audire, scriberem sine molestia;<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">Vgl. ebd., Z. 42-44.</note> quia vero utilitatem quo<lb xml:id="p1z6"/>que expetis, tacendum puto.</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Ego quidem illud inde nactus sum, ut magis timeam <placeName ref="l832">Gallos</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>et firmetur hoc apud me, quod quidam<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">Unbekannt.</note> olim scripsit: monstra fovere<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Vgl. Adagia, 2, 4, 98 (<bibl source="b370">LB</bibl> II 551).</note> <placeName ref="l832">Galliam</placeName><note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6">Dies in Umkehrung einer Äußerung von Hieronymus (Contra Vigilantium, 1; <bibl source="b446">MPL</bibl> XXIII 355): "Sola Gallia monstra non habuit."</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z8"/>De <persName ref="p8397">Clausero</persName><note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7"><persName ref="p8397">Christoph Klauser</persName>; vgl. oben <ref target="file11797">Nr. 1751</ref>, 22-25.</note> nihil non dixit parochus in <placeName ref="l70">Buͦbiken</placeName><note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8"><persName ref="p3067">Johannes Stumpf</persName>, Pfarrer in <placeName ref="l70">Bubikon</placeName>.</note> - nuper enim hac transiit -, ita non est <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>opus nosse me plura.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Erit mihi exemplo vir ille, quousque vixero.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Vita nanque eius <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>cum fuerit mihi notissima, non potui satis admirari, quod accidit.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Videmus hinc, quanto <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>cum studio sit ambulandum in timore domini.</s>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la">Hunc ego rogo, ut illum restituat ac pro<lb xml:id="p1z12"/>tegat in futurum.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la"><persName ref="p467">Bucerus</persName> expectatur in singulos dies; ad tempus sex mensium <persName ref="p8374">Hedio</persName> <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>succedet,<note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">Vgl. oben <ref target="file11797">Nr. 1751</ref>, 13 mit Anm. 7.</note> ut ille queat interim quiescere, quamvis mihi videatur <persName ref="p467">Bucerum</persName> non discessurum <lb xml:id="p1z14"/><placeName ref="l56">Bonna</placeName>, donec alter praesens sit.</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la">Quod igitur ad tuas<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10">Die Rede ist vom nicht erhaltenen Brief <persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName>, auf den <persName ref="p467">Bucer</persName> am 21. Juli antwortete (s. unten <ref target="file11809">Nr. 1763</ref>).</note> adtinet, recte agam.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z15"/>Quia vero de <persName ref="p18538">cęsaris</persName><note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11"><persName ref="p18538">Karl V.</persName></note> impietate nunquam non audio, fere sum in ea opinione, qua <lb xml:id="p1z16"/><persName ref="p8011">Rodulphus</persName><note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12"><persName ref="p8011">Rudolf Gwalther</persName>.</note> noster, <placeName ref="l822">Germanię</placeName> nihil esse allaturum boni<note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13">Siehe <persName ref="p8011">Gwalther</persName> an <persName ref="p8418">Myconius</persName>, 6. Mai 1543, <placeName ref="l473">St. Gallen</placeName> Kantonsbibliothek (Vadiana), Ms 34 (VBS V), 186r.: "Ego certe credo caesarem non sine divina providentia hoc damni in Germaniae foribus accepisse, qui haud dubie, si posset, daret nobis, qui Christum profitemur, magnum aliquod malum."</note>.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la">Ob eius adventum aiunt bellum <lb xml:id="p1z17"/>a <persName ref="p18605">Iuliacensi</persName><note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14">Herzog <persName ref="p18605">Wilhelm von Jülich-Berg-Kleve-Geldern</persName>.</note> instauratum.</s>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l760">Salodori</placeName><note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" n="15">In <placeName ref="l760">Solothurn</placeName>.</note> narratur <persName ref="p20225">Gallum</persName><note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16">König <persName ref="p20225">Franz I.</persName></note> in <placeName ref="l2589">Picardia</placeName> habere congregatum <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>exercitum usque ad centum millia<note xml:id="fn17" type="footnote" n="17">Zur Aufstellung eines <placeName ref="l832">französischen</placeName> Heeres in der <placeName ref="l2589">Picardie</placeName> vgl. <bibl source="b194">Du Bellay, Mémoires</bibl> IV 124-131; <bibl source="b301">Henne</bibl> VIII 104-109.</note>.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la">Ibidem pro certo ferunt <persName ref="p20225">Gallum</persName> nunciasse comiti <lb xml:id="p1z19"/><persName ref="p7492">Gulielmo</persName><note xml:id="fn18" type="footnote" n="18"><persName ref="p7492">Wilhelm von Fürstenberg</persName>.</note>, quod, ubiubi in manus suas deveniat, lentissima morte perempturum esse <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>atque id suspendio; comitem contra: debere regem cavere, se enim perrecturum in proposito <lb xml:id="p1z21"/>cęsaris ministerio et, ubicunque nactus ipsum fuerit, eo genere mortis usurum esse, <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>quo ipse sit usus in hunc usque diem contra evangelicos.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la">Comparantur aliquot vexilla cir<lb xml:id="p1z23"/>cum nos militum, qui obviam eant cęsari<pb type="edition" next="160"/> atque deducant nescio quo.</s>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la">Per <placeName ref="l2459">Rhenum</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>demisisse fertur bombardos maiores 108<note xml:id="fna" type="footnote" n="a"><hi>In der Vorlage</hi> c et viij.</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z25"/><persName ref="p18477">Ferdinandus</persName> rex praesidium quęrit mittendum <placeName ref="l546">Viennensibus</placeName>; timet enim obsidionem.</s>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la">Fuit <lb xml:id="p1z26"/>his diebus hic <persName ref="p7780">dux ex Louffenberga</persName>,<note xml:id="fn19" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="19">Gemeint ist sicher <persName ref="p7780">Hans Othmar von Schönau</persName>, gest. 1554, seit 1539 Vogt von <placeName ref="l3238">Laufenburg</placeName> und Hauptmann der <placeName ref="l3239">Vier Waldstädte</placeName>, der bereits 1529 unter den Verteidigern <placeName ref="l546">Wiens</placeName> gegen die <placeName ref="l2510">Türken</placeName> war. - Lit.: Adel an Ober- und Hochrhein. Beiträge zur Geschichte der Freiherren von Schönau, hg. v. Wernher Freiherr von Schönau-Wehr und Katharina Frings, Freiburg i. Br. 2001, passim (bes. S. 85. 192. 363f. 373f).</note> non postremus eorum, quibus illuc eundum est.</s>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="la">Idem <lb xml:id="p1z27"/>adseruit sex millia <placeName ref="l834">Italorum</placeName> iam esse in itinere <placeName ref="l546">Viennam</placeName> versus<note xml:id="fn20" type="footnote" n="20">Zu den Werbungen König <persName ref="p18477">Ferdinands</persName> in <placeName ref="l834">Italien</placeName> vgl. <bibl source="b480">PC</bibl> III 383.</note>.</s>
					<s n="24" xml:lang="la">Hi sunt rumore<lb xml:id="p1z28"/>s bellorum; at nondum est finis.</s>
					<s n="25" xml:lang="la">Non ferior ita rumoribus istis, ut quod evangelium tam <lb xml:id="p1z29"/>sine honore habetur apud nos.</s>
					<s n="26" xml:lang="la">Auditoria sunt frequentissima; fructus, quos videas, nulli, <lb xml:id="p1z30"/>flagitiorum omnia plaena.</s>
					<s n="27" xml:lang="la">Et profecto, dum rem sanis oculis intueor, e nobis quidam <lb xml:id="p1z31"/>ad istam infelicitatem non parum conferunt<note xml:id="fn21" type="footnote" n="21"><persName ref="p8418">Myconius</persName> spielt wohl konkret auf die Verhältnisse in <placeName ref="l28">Basel</placeName> an, könnte aber auch die Protestanten insgesamt meinen.</note>.</s>
					<s n="28" xml:lang="la">Dominus Iesus nos emendet.</s>
					<s n="29" xml:lang="la">Amen.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="30" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">Val<lb xml:id="p1z32"/>e cum tuis omnibus in domino.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="31" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l28">Basileę</placeName>, 21. iunii anno 1543.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="32" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z33"/><persName ref="p8418">Os. Myconius</persName> <lb xml:id="p1z34"/>tuus.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="33" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Domino <persName ref="p495">Henricho Bullingero</persName> <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>optimo atque doctissimo, <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>in domino suo.</s>
					<s n="34" xml:lang="de"><placeName ref="l587">Z[ürich]</placeName><note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>Teilweise auf das nicht mehr vorhandene Verschlussband geschrieben.</hi></note>.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
	</text>
